---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

// Deliberately not linked from the site navigation. It is reachable only by
// people who have the URL, and carries the same noindex tag as every other
// page while the site is under review.
const pageTitle = `For your review | ${SITE_TITLE}`;
const description = 'A short guide to reviewing the preserved Bobby Albert archive.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={pageTitle} description={description} />
		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
				max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
				margin: auto;
			}
			.lede {
				font-size: 1.1em;
			}
			.q {
				border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
				padding: 0.1em 0 0.1em 1em;
				margin: 1.5em 0;
			}
			.q p:first-child {
				font-weight: 700;
				margin-bottom: 0.3em;
			}
			.q p:last-child {
				margin-bottom: 0;
			}
			.note {
				background: rgba(var(--gray-light), 45%);
				border-radius: 8px;
				padding: 1em 1.2em;
			}
			ul {
				padding-left: 1.2em;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>For your review</h1>

			<p class="lede">
				Bobby &mdash; this site preserves your blog and your True North Business guides so
				they stay available to anyone looking for them. Nothing here is final. Please look
				it over and tell us what to change.
			</p>

			<div class="note">
				<p>
					<strong>This site is currently hidden from Google and other search engines.</strong>{' '}
					Anyone with the link can read it, but it will not turn up in search results until
					you say you are happy for it to.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2>What is here</h2>

			<ul>
				<li>
					<a href="/blog/">289 blog posts</a>, published between 2014 and 2022, with their
					original dates, web addresses and images.
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href="/resources/true-north-business/">12 True North Business guides</a>, each
					readable on the page with the original PDF available to download.
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href="/about/">An About page</a> drawn from your own writing.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Questions we need you to answer</h2>

			<div class="q">
				<p>1. Are you happy for the True North Business guides to be free?</p>
				<p>
					All twelve are on the site now, readable by anyone, with no email address
					required. Several of them were originally offered in exchange for contact
					details. This is your call, and it is the most important question on this page.{' '}
					<a href="/resources/true-north-business/">See the guides &rarr;</a>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="q">
				<p>2. Is there anything here that should not be public?</p>
				<p>
					Any post, guide or photograph can be removed. If something is out of date, was
					written for a business that no longer operates, or you would simply rather it
					were not online, say so and it will come down.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="q">
				<p>3. Six tables were rebuilt from an internet archive &mdash; are they right?</p>
				<p>
					Tables in six posts were lost when the original site was taken down, and were
					recovered from an archived copy. You would know better than anyone whether they
					are correct. The most important are in{' '}
					<a href="/blog/truth-about-leading-and-managing/">The Truth About Leading and Managing</a>,{' '}
					<a href="/blog/the-greatest-leadership-gap/">The Greatest Leadership Gap</a> and{' '}
					<a href="/blog/6-reasons-why-your-customers-are-leaving/">6 Reasons Why Your Customers Are Leaving</a>.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="q">
				<p>4. Does the About page sound like you?</p>
				<p>
					It was taken from your own words, but it is short, and the photograph was chosen
					for you. <a href="/about/">Read it &rarr;</a>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="q">
				<p>5. Where should this live?</p>
				<p>
					The site sits at a temporary web address at the moment. Your own domain,
					bobbyalbert.com, currently points somewhere else. Let us know what you would
					like the permanent address to be.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2>What is not here yet</h2>

			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Your podcast episodes.</strong> Around 90 episodes of True North
					Leader, True North Business and Lead2Grow are not on the site. Tell us if you
					would like them preserved too.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>The True North Culture and True North Leader guides.</strong> Only the
					Business set has been added so far.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>One table could not be recovered.</strong> Everything else that was lost
					has been restored.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>How to give feedback</h2>

			<p>
				There is no need to be technical about it. A list of notes is perfect &mdash; the page
				you were looking at, and what you would like changed. Small wording changes are quick;
				so is removing anything you would rather was not there.
			</p>

			<p><a href="/">&larr; Back to the site</a></p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
